# AI Orchestrator

Supports `.project-overview.mdc` and `architecture.mdc`. AI is a **Python service** (`apps/ai`), not a TypeScript implementation.

The TypeScript modular monolith remains the core application. `apps/api/src/modules/ai` is **only** the integration boundary required to talk to Python.

## TypeScript integration boundary

Allowed in `apps/api`:

```
modules/ai/
  application/ports/AIServicePort
  adapters/outbound/python-ai/PythonAIServiceAdapter
```

Plus versionable DTO / API / event contracts (`packages/contracts`).

TypeScript must NOT contain or depend on: OpenAI SDK, Anthropic SDK, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, embedding SDKs, vector database SDKs for AI, prompt orchestration, or AI agents.

## Python layout

```
apps/ai/
├── app/
│   ├── domain/
│   ├── application/
│   ├── adapters/
│   ├── agents/
│   ├── orchestration/
│   ├── rag/
│   ├── llm/
│   ├── embeddings/
│   ├── vector_store/
│   ├── tools/
│   ├── prompts/
│   ├── guardrails/
│   ├── evaluation/
│   └── main.py
├── tests/
├── pyproject.toml
└── README.md
```

Stack: Python, FastAPI, Pydantic, async where appropriate.

Hexagonal direction: **Adapters → Application → Domain**. Domain, application, agents, orchestration, RAG, prompts, tools, and guardrails must not import FastAPI, LangChain, LangGraph, LlamaIndex, OpenAI, Anthropic, or other provider SDKs. FastAPI belongs in inbound adapters only.

Provider SDKs live only under adapters (choose later; do not install every provider now):

```
apps/ai/app/adapters/
├── llm/openai/
├── llm/anthropic/
├── llm/ollama/
├── embeddings/
└── vector_store/
```

Python naming: snake_case files (`generate_ai_response.py`); class names stay business-specific (`GenerateAIResponseUseCase`, `LLMPort`, `OpenAILLMAdapter`).

## Communication

**Synchronous HTTP** — TypeScript API → FastAPI. Use for AI response generation, classification, summarization, AI decisions.

**Asynchronous** — TypeScript → event bus / queue → Python worker → event → TypeScript. Use for document processing, embeddings, RAG ingestion, long-running AI, batch AI.

```
Conversation (TS) → AIServicePort → PythonAIServiceAdapter
  → Python inbound → application / orchestration / agents
  → LLMPort / EmbeddingPort / VectorSearchPort → provider adapter
```

Do not share Python or TypeScript internals. Use explicit contracts. `apps/ai` must remain independently deployable.

## Allowed in Python AI

AI orchestration, agents, RAG, embeddings, vector search, LLM integrations, prompts, tools, guardrails, classification, summarization, sentiment, escalation recommendations, AI evaluation/testing.

## Forbidden

- Any of the above AI implementation in `apps/api` or `apps/web`
- Python AI → Prisma / TypeScript business database
- AI mutating Conversation/Ticket aggregates directly
- Unvalidated model output entering TypeScript domain logic
- Cross-tenant retrieval
- Installing or wiring every LLM provider “just in case”

Correct: Python AI → Decision/result → TypeScript business use case → Domain → Event.

## Tool calling

Tools are an explicit allowlist: `getCustomerDetails`, `getOrderDetails`, `createTicket`, `updateTicket`, `checkRefundStatus`, `handoffToAgent`.

```
Python LLM → tool request → TypeScript validates → authorize
  → TypeScript application use case → domain → tool result → Python LLM
```

Never give the model database, Redis, or raw infrastructure access. Mutating tools run only in TypeScript.

## Tenant context

Every AI/RAG request and event must carry tenant context from TypeScript. Python must never retrieve across tenants.

## Extraction

`apps/ai` is a separate service boundary. Keep its public surface as HTTP / queue / event contracts plus application use cases. Do not fold AI back into the Node process.
